# A sandbox's /dev/null mount over a protected path (0087). Inside the sandbox git sees a
# character device, which peal_status_porcelain already filters (0084). Once the sandbox
# is gone — a plain host process, or this same worktree later — the same path is an
# ordinary empty regular file, and nothing tells it apart from a real one someone added on
# purpose. Rather than guess, these are the paths a sandbox has actually mounted over, from
# the untracked list of 912623c (0057), anchored to the repository root so an unrelated
# file of the same name elsewhere (e.g. under a subproject) is unaffected. A tracked file
# is never hidden by this: check `git ls-files` before adding a name.
/.bash_profile
/.bashrc
/.claude/agents
/.claude/commands
/.claude/hooks
/.claude/launch.json
/.claude/loop.md
/.claude/output-styles
/.claude/routines
/.claude/scheduled_tasks.json
/.claude/settings.local.json
/.claude/skills
/.claude/workflows
/.gitconfig
/.gitmodules
/.idea
/.mcp.json
/.profile
/.ripgreprc
/.vscode
/.zprofile
/.zshrc
